-- title:
--   The bits of the downsized vector are its coordinates' Shoup bits, in the numbering
-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Background.AnswerReduction.Layout` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). The layout of the PCP coordinates. Piece AR-3d of `planning/answer-reduction.md`: how a program reads a vector of `V^pcp`. * The coordinates are numbered in three runs (`coordIndex`): the concatenated point register `V_{6,pt}` (`pt6`, `m'` coordinates), the concatenated direction register `V_{6,dir}` (`dir6`), and the six seeds. A vector of `V^pcp` is thus the three lists `ptOf6`, `dirOf6`, `seedsOf`. * Each copy of the test is a contiguous run of `V_{6,pt}` and of `V_{6,dir}` with its own seed (`regsAt`): copy `i ≤ 5` at offset `i·m` and length `m` (`regs_eq`), copy `6` at offset `0` and…
--
--   **The bits of the downsized vector** are its coordinates' Shoup bits, in the numbering.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.AnswerReduction
--   open MIPRE.AnswerReduction.Pcp
--   open Finset MIPRE.LIDT MIPRE.LIDT.CL MIPRE.SAT MIPRE.CL MIPRE.Cost
--   variable (P : PcpParams)
--   variable {F : Type*}
--   variable {k : ℕ} (hk : 1 ≤ k)
--
--   theorem MIPRE.AnswerReduction.Pcp.toBits_pcp (v : Coord P → (shoupBinField k hk).carrier) :
--       toBits (reindexEquiv (bitIndex P k) (downsizeEquiv (shoupPowerBasis k hk) v)) =
--         flatBits P hk v
--   ```
